{"id": "tpcds-005", "level": "expert", "nl_description": "Schema for a retail decision support benchmark with three sales channels: physical stores, online (web), and catalog mail-order. Shared conformed dimensions: DATE_DIM (73,049 rows, covers 1900-2100, includes full calendar and fiscal attributes, d_holiday and d_weekend boolean flags), TIME_DIM (86,400 rows, one per second, shift and meal-time annotations), ITEM (18K rows per SF, SCD type-2 with rec_start_date and rec_end_date, 10 categories, log-normally distributed current price with log-mean 3.5 and log-std 1.2), CUSTOMER (100K rows per SF, linked to two demographic tables and an address table), CUSTOMER_DEMOGRAPHICS (1.92M rows, combinatoric of gender, marital status, education level), HOUSEHOLD_DEMOGRAPHICS (7200 rows, cross of income band and household size), CUSTOMER_ADDRESS, STORE (12 per SF), WAREHOUSE (5 per SF), SHIP_MODE (20 modes), PROMOTION (300 per SF), REASON (55 rows). Store sales is the largest fact table (~2.9M rows per SF). Each sale line carries 23 columns including quantity uniform in [1,100], list price, sales price, wholesale cost, extended amounts, coupon amount, net paid, net profit. Store returns (~287K) reference the originating ticket. Web and catalog channels have analogous fact/return tables. Each channel fact also has a promo FK.", "ground_truth_schema": {"tables": [{"name": "DATE_DIM", "pk": "d_date_sk", "columns": [{"name": "d_date_sk", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_date_id", "data_type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "d_date", "data_type": "DATE"}, {"name": "d_month_seq", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_week_seq", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_quarter_seq", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_dow", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_moy", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_dom", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_qoy", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_fy_year", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_fy_quarter_seq", "data_type": "INT"}, {"name": "d_fy_we